@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Typed channel-event extraction (no analysis-time parsing)

skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFC
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #343A40
  FontColor #212529
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
  BorderColor #495057
}

component "Caller-owned Tree-sitter tree\nRholang or another frontend" as TREE #DBE4FF
component "NodeMapper frontend boundary\ngrammar kind → CpgNodeKind + MsgKind" as MAP #FFE8CC
component "Unified CodePropertyGraph\nAST · Function scopes · SourceRange" as CPG #C3FAE8
component "Typed identity evidence\nIdentifier.definition\nDefUse · ReachingDef · Reference" as DFG #FFF3BF
component "Top-level process discovery\nstop before nested Function" as SCOPE #D3F9D8
component "Statement-local resolver\nskip nested event subtrees\ncanonical candidate order" as RESOLVE #E5DBFF
component "BTreeMap<NodeId, Vec<ChannelEvent>>\nprocess and site order" as EVENTS #FCC2D7
component "Unresolved event\nchannel = None" as UNKNOWN #F1F3F5

TREE --> MAP : one parse
MAP --> CPG : attach normalized metadata
CPG --> SCOPE : Function + AstChild
SCOPE --> RESOLVE : ordered event sites
DFG --> RESOLVE : semantic identity only
RESOLVE --> EVENTS : resolved Variable NodeId
RESOLVE --> UNKNOWN : insufficient evidence
UNKNOWN --> EVENTS : retain uncertainty

note bottom of MAP
  Concrete tokens (<-, <=, <<-, !?) are interpreted here.
  The feature-free analyzer never scans source text.
end note

note bottom of EVENTS
  Extraction is read-only. Every emitted site/range is copied from the CPG.
end note

legend bottom
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DBE4FF>| caller-owned parse evidence |
|<#FFE8CC>| language-specific normalization boundary |
|<#C3FAE8>| unified CPG storage |
|<#FFF3BF>| typed definition/reference evidence |
|<#D3F9D8>| process scope selection |
|<#E5DBFF>| deterministic channel resolution |
|<#FCC2D7>| ordered public events |
|<#F1F3F5>| explicit missing evidence |
endlegend
@enduml
